{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1355681-what-do-you-guys-think-of-the-straussen-academy","id":1355681,"title":"What do you guys think of the Straussen Academy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-18T13:07:37-08:00","id":1355681,"title":"What do you guys think of the Straussen Academy?","content":"I forget what book it's in, but the Straussen Academy is a boarding school somewhere in New England that educates and helps Awaken the chlldren of Hermetic magi and other Tradition mages. Have any of you used it? I'm trying to convince our ST to let my character be a student or a recent graduate of the Straussen Academy if we end up playing Mage instead of Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T13:58:10-08:00","id":1355693,"title":"","content":"It's in the Revised Order of Hermes Tradition Book, pp. 78-84.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T15:41:52-08:00","id":1355704,"title":"","content":"To me sounds like a Harry Potter adaptation. I think that the relationship between mentor and student is inherently individual, the Academy is noted as an exception, an interesting one may be. But a dangerous risk to draw the attention of the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T20:14:08-08:00","id":1355750,"title":"","content":"I feel like they wanted to do something akin to Harry Potter, and paid some lip-service to the idea, but sort of failed. What I find truly remarkable is that they were able to bite off Harry Potter (the most Reader's Digest facsimile of Hogwarts-as-premise anyway), but completely avoid putting in any of the stuff that makes Hogwarts or Harry Potter <i>fun;</i> or really <i>any </i>of the fun parts of various books, shows, movies, and cartoons that revolve around a boarding school for supernaturals/demigods/the children of Disney characters/spies/super heroes/mutants/etc. I mean, I would have understood them not doing at all because the elements that make that setting cool and fun are more appropriate for a Changeling game than anything else--and that's assuming such a setting even has a place in the World of Darkness in the first place, given it's purportedly dark undertones and mood. But I think that once you decide to do it, then I think you nee to REALLY do it: pay full homage to the tropes that make those settings compelling or engaging in the first place, regardless of whether it fits with whatever else.<br /> <br /> Having said that, I think a 2nd Ed.-era game set around Doissetep, but where people play low-Arete mages still in training, would be well served and a lot of fun if run in a manner that took its dramatic and narrative cues from the likes of <i>The Magicians </i>and <i>The Paper Chase</i> (the movie not the show.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":2319,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","user":"CaptOtter","date":". 12-18-2019, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T01:04:52-08:00","id":1355791,"title":"","content":"I agree, Doissetep and Horizon had greater success in capture the mood of a school of fantasy. On the other hand, Harry Potter is very very similar to Neil Gaiman comics Books of Magic. And they were probably the influence behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T10:18:52-08:00","id":1355884,"title":"","content":"Supposedly Rowling did not read <i>The Books of Magic</i> before writing Harry Potter. All the similarities were coincidences. Supposedly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T07:49:29-08:00","id":1356094,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24202_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24202\" data-vbnamecard=\"24202\">Justycar</a> good point about the risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T09:34:24-08:00","id":1357555,"title":"","content":"I've read about the Straussen Academy. Given they had what, 6 pages to work with, I think it's OK as an idea. At the same time, young Magi can do almost nothing evocative or dramatic with level 1 spheres. All you can do is &quot;sense&quot; things. Part of what makes Harry Potter more interesting is the ability to master a specific spell. The simple idea of transfiguring a piece of paper into a Mouse is what, Life 4/Matter 4? A lot of the &quot;interesting&quot; effects in Mage require a shit ton of spheres and mastery... Which technically take decades to learn.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T11:11:58-08:00","id":1357573,"title":"","content":"I ended up creating a Tytalus mage who recently graduated from Straussen and the ST said that was fine, she was cool with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T13:12:42-08:00","id":1357871,"title":"","content":"Straussen Academy isn't Hogwarts by a long shot: first and most significantly, almost none of its students are, were, or will be wizards. As such, the Academy didn't teach magic. Apparently, it doesn't even teach sorcery. It <i>does</i> inculcate the students with (in M20 terms) the Hermetic Focus, which would make them the Hermetic equivalent of Extraordinary Citizens, able to actually use Hermetic Talismans and, more importantly, influence Reality Zones to be more favorable to the Hermetic ways. <br /> <br /> That said, I would definitely put a Primer in the Academy's library, and make its study part of the standard coursework. And in my take on the Mage setting, there would be what I call Spellbooks there, too:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T15:06:02-08:00","id":1357888,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}